    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem is that connection feels like a lie now. i spent so long convincing myself that people were the source of all my problems, and i was right. any attempt to \"step out\" feels like I'm just inviting the chaos back in. it's like i've finally reached the end of a long road and there's just nothing there for me. just this heavy, endless weight. it feels more like a dead end than a starting point.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's as if you've built walls around yourself to protect against the hurt you felt, and now those walls feel impenetrable. The connection you're seeking is not object-based, but relational, and that takes vulnerability and trust, which feels almost unimaginable after everything you've been through. It might take some time to rebuild that trust, but the idea of being alone with a heavy burden doesn't have to be a dead end; it can be a chance to rediscover yourself and find new strength.",
      "source": "target",
